  "lineage": "Goze were blind women who travelled in small groups through the villages of Echigo, in present-day Niigata, singing to the shamisen at farmhouses in return for lodging and rice, with their main guilds based in Takada and Nagaoka. Their repertoire included the long narrative saimon matsuzaka, kudoki ballads and folk songs, and Kobayashi Haru, the last Nagaoka goze, and the Takada goze were recorded from the 1970s.",
